kibana-plugin/node_modules

# SEC-CC-1: premium PLAINTEXT must never enter the image — only the sealed
# blob (poc/backend/premium/*.sealed) is copied in (sealed before the build).
**/premium_src

# Developer scratch copies. `.gitignore` alone is NOT enough: a pattern ignored
# by git still exists in the working tree, and the working tree is the docker
# build context. Two such files shipped in every image —
# backend/license_verifier.py.fork-pre-converge and
# backend/rstlic_client.py.fork-pre-converge — carrying, in readable Python, the
# token wire format and verification path that the Cython stage exists to
# obfuscate. Any gitignore-only pattern does the same, so match broadly.
**/*.fork-pre-converge
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/*.bak
**/*~

# Test and evaluation material. Shipping the suite publishes internal test
# expectations and eval fixtures to anyone who can `docker cp`, which
# contradicts obfuscating the backend at all. `main.py` writes
# eval/failed_cases.yaml at runtime, so the directory is recreated then — the
# shipped copies are not needed.
**/tests
**/eval

